{#
compose/_sending.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The answer to a send, and it changes nothing on screen.

That is the point of it. Every earlier version of this response took the
window away — the dock's closed into a toast carrying an Undo link, the
inline one was replaced by a countdown bar in the thread — so the cancel was
always offered somewhere other than where the user had just clicked, and the
window had to be rebuilt from scratch to get it back. The window now stays,
its Send pill reads "Sending… click to cancel" for the whole cancel window,
and this stream's only job is to hand it the two things it cannot know by
itself:

  • `undoUrl`   — how to call the send off. Addressed by the message id, which
                  for a message composed and sent without an autosave is
                  minted by the send itself, so it cannot be baked into the
                  window at render time.
  • `settleUrl` — how to tidy up when the offer expires: put the sent message
                  in the conversation and take the window away. See
                  ComposeController::sent().

Appended into the frame rather than replacing anything, and it takes itself
back out as soon as it has spoken — see compose--send-hold.

Variables: ctx, undoUrl, settleUrl, cancelWindow
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="{{ ctx.frame }}">
    <template>
        <div hidden
             data-controller="compose--send-hold"
             data-compose--send-hold-undo-url-value="{{ undoUrl }}"
             data-compose--send-hold-settle-url-value="{{ settleUrl }}"
             data-compose--send-hold-delay-value="{{ cancelWindow }}"></div>
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
